{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmfX6Eo6hrQ8sZR8J2L7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done reading. I stopped at the glossary (screen 8) and didn't open screen 9.\n\n**What I'd tell my friend:** Yes, keep it, it's worth it. It's a savings pot. I put in a bit from my salary and my employer puts in more. After **6 years** from the first deposit I can take it all out with no tax, or after 3 years if I'm near retirement age. I can take it out earlier, but then they take tax. I'm fairly sure. What decided it was the bar chart: \"הפקדתם 18,000 ₪\" and \"המעסיק הוסיף +54,000 ₪\". Even when I pulled it out early at 5 years and lost \"‎−13,974 ₪\" in tax, \"נשאר בידיים 66,513 ₪\". From my 18,000 that's a lot. First step: ask HR which company runs mine and which track I'm in. The page lists tracks like \"מדד S&P 500\", and moving between tracks has no tax.\n\n**How it went:**\n- **Screen 1:** The heading \"קרן השתלמות\" was exactly what I came for. I read \"אחרי 6 שנים… אפשר למשוך את הכסף בלי מס הכנסה ובלי מס רווחי הון\". If you take it before 6 years, you pay tax, \"לפחות 31%\".\n- **Screen 2:** I saw \"למה משתמשים בזה\": for employees it's usually the first step. I saw the track chips (S&P 500, מסלול כללי…). Then there were tabs, \"שכירים\" / \"עצמאים\", already set on שכירים.\n- **Screen 3:** This is where it clicked. The big chart with 18,000, +54,000 and 66,513. I didn't touch the slider.\n- **Screen 4:** Small text with a scary \"47% מס\". I skipped it. I also skipped the \"שחקו עם המספרים שלכם\" fold and the \"שווה לדעת\" list.\n- **Screen 5:** \"מתי הכסף פנוי: כשעוברות 6 שנים\", money arrives within \"עד 4 ימי עסקים\", and moving to another fund is \"בלי מס\".\n- **Screen 6:** Fees are \"עד 2% בשנה\" and there's no exit fee. The tax cards I skimmed.\n- **Screen 7:** The orange warning that taking it early is expensive. I didn't really read the rest.\n- **Screen 8:** A glossary. That's where I closed it.\n\n**Where I got confused:**\n- The early-withdrawal tax: is it 31% or 47%? Two different numbers in two places.\n- Is the 66,513 what I get after 5 years, or the 12-year number? I think it's 5, because \"5 שנים\" was marked.\n- Is 2% a lot? I don't know. It's a percent and not in shekels, so I didn't worry about it much.\n- I didn't understand \"הפקדה מוטבת\", \"רווח ריאלי\", \"ותק\", \"משכורת קובעת\" or \"גמל להשקעה\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1885,"cache_read_input_tokens":17524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1885},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"279865b3-b503-4c9c-92c8-06f6aa8db93b","uuid":"60de0e9d-9e93-4b17-b091-bde36f7c14e3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T12:21:19.222Z","request_id":"req_011CgmfX61tiTmk47VePnHJ1"}
